  <figcaption>
    The behavior-alignment loop can start from human intent or a passing test.
    EARS and Gherkin are optional at runtime; the stable <code>@flow:</code>
    identity joins readable behavior to the runtime-verification loop. An
    <strong>effect</strong> is a database, API, cache, or messaging action.
    <strong>ODC</strong> asks whether different code-decision outcomes produced
    distinguishable effects.
  </figcaption>
